{
    "background_story": "Luka grew up in a small, secluded village surrounded by lush forests and rolling hills. His community lived in harmony with nature, relying on traditional farming and craftsmanship to sustain themselves. Luka's family was known for their exceptional woodworking skills, passed down through generations. He spent most of his days learning the art of woodworking from his father, using hand tools and locally sourced materials to create beautiful, functional pieces. As the world outside became increasingly industrialized, Luka's village remained a tranquil oasis, untouched by the hum of machines. He took great pride in preserving the traditional ways of his ancestors, and his handmade creations were highly sought after by those seeking unique, non-industrial pieces. Luka's commitment to his craft and his community's way of life kept the spirit of simplicity and sustainability alive.",
